§ `Route-α variadic construction: what does NOT fire (SET-OPERATORS-SPEC §D7.1)`

-- The rewrite is deliberately narrow: record constructors with exactly one
-- LIST-typed field, at two or more arguments. Everything below must remain
-- an error, locking in the conservative-extension boundary.

DECLARE Bag OF a
  HAS items IS A LIST OF a

DECLARE Tag OF a
  HAS label IS A STRING
      value IS AN a

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
      xs IS A LIST OF a
GIVETH A Bag OF a
mkBag xs MEANS Bag OF xs

-- one argument that is not a list: never rewritten (no singleton sugar)
oneArg MEANS Bag OF 5

-- a two-field constructor over-applied: not a single-list-field shape
overApplied MEANS Tag OF "x", 1, 2

-- an ordinary FUNCTION with a list parameter: constructors only
fnApplied MEANS mkBag OF 1, 2, 3
